# The snapshot's last promised member: available actions. An automation lane
# asks what the app will DO right now and gets the same list a person sees in
# the `>` palette, in the same order, resolvable by the same label through
# `act`. One catalog (App::available_actions), three readers.
# Offline; FRESH profile.
settle 30
key escape

# The static registry is on offer from the start.
assert snap actions ~ Fit view
assert snap actions ~ Open Gloss pane

# And a label the snapshot reports is a label `act` can resolve — the
# round trip that makes the list worth publishing.
act Fit view
settle 10

# Contextual rows JOIN the catalog when their context exists, and they LEAD
# it: summoning a Gloss adds that pane's own composition rows.
act Open Gloss pane
settle 15
assert pane gloss
assert snap actions ~ Gloss: add section

# The contextual row resolves through the same `act` verb as a static one...
act Gloss: add section — Removed
settle 10
assert event pane-section-added removed

# ...and the catalog tracks the state change: the row is now the REMOVE form,
# so what the snapshot offers is what the app will actually do next.
assert snap actions ~ Gloss: remove section — Removed
capture 01_catalog_with_contextual_rows

log available actions receipt complete
